<title>USA: U.S. hope for heat build may lie in Asia - analysts.</title>
<headline>U.S. hope for heat build may lie in Asia - analysts.</headline>
<byline>Oliver Ludwig</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Energy Secretary Hazel O'Leary may be looking south to Venezuela for help in easing heating oil price spikes this winter, but some analysts reckon relief is more likely to come from the east.</p>
<p>A massive expansion of refining capacity throughout Asia this year will free up larger and larger volumes of heating oil and may ease the tight world distillate market which has led to dwindling inventories, they said.</p>
<p>&quot;I still believe there's time to build (U.S.) stocks,&quot; said Nizam Sharief, analyst at Hornsby &amp; Co in Houston.</p>
</text>
